   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Saddle Rock Minyan to file an application\nfor retroactive real property tax exemption",
    "basePrintNo": "S6797",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6797-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6797\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing Saddle Rock Minyan to file an applica-\ntion for retroactive real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation authorizes Saddle Rock Minyan to file for an exemption\nfor real property taxes with respect to the 2021-2022 and 2022-2023\nassessment rolls\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes. the Saddle Rock Minyan to file for an exemption\nfor real property taxes with respect to the 2021-2022 and 2022-2023\nassessment rolls for relevant general and school taxes.  This is for the\nproperty located at 115 Greenleaf Hill, in the incorporated village of\nSaddle Rock, town of North Hempstead, County of Nassau otherwise known\nas district 007, section 02, block 318, lot 60.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Saddle Rock Minyan to file for an\nexemption for real property taxes for a parcel that has been granted an\nexemption going forward.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
